Role of Small Business in Socio,
Economic Development of India
Output Generation:
Small industries in India
contribute almost 40% of
gross industrial value added
and 45% of total exports
from India.
Employment Generation:
After agriculture, small
industries are the second
largest employers of human
resources in India.They use
more labour intensive
techniques and less capital
intensive techniques. This is
a blessing for labour surplus
country like India.
Balanced Regional Development:
Small industries producing
simple products, using
simple technologies, depend
on locally available resources
so these can be set up
anywhere in the country.
Since they can be widely
spread, thus contribute
significantly to the balanced
development of the country.
